From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saifuddin Hitawala <hitawala@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:47:07 -0800
Subject: [gpu] Check SubmitIfNecessary before clear in
 RasterDecoder/CopySIHelper

Check return value of SubmitIfNecessary before calling SetCleared in
places where clear happens in RasterDecoder and CopySharedImageHelper.
This translates to updating success bool in all these places as it
already stores result of FlushWriteAccess.

Bug: 568937157
Cq-Exclude-Trybots: luci.chromium.try:dawn-win10-x86-deps-rel
Change-Id: Ie1039ab31d68d28c47bbb58b557ecb51edf3730e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8704260
Reviewed-by: Kyle Charbonneau <kylechar@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Saifuddin Hitawala <hitawala@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1734357}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
DoWritePixelsINTERNAL() on this branch did not store the FlushWriteAccess()
result; `success` is introduced there and used to guard SetCleared() and the
return value, matching upstream.

